# Every variable this service reads, and nothing else.
#
# Rule 9 of docs/ecosystem/03 §2: a repository declares the variables it needs and the deploy
# provides exactly those. `env_file: .env` fan-out — which hands every container the whole estate's
# secrets — is banned, and this file is what makes the alternative possible.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local work. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way.

# --- required --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# This service's own database. It reads no other, and CI fails on a second connection string.
TRADE_DATABASE_URL=postgres://trade:trade@127.0.0.1:5432/trade

# Identity's JWKS and issuer. Token verification is the only thing this service asks identity for.
IDENTITY_JWKS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4001/.well-known/jwks.json
IDENTITY_ISSUER=http://127.0.0.1:4001

# HMAC key for event signatures — outbound AND INBOUND.
#
# This is the key that verifies `identity.user.deleted` on POST /v1/events. An erasure webhook with
# no MAC is a delete-anyone endpoint: anyone who can reach the port can erase a user's bots. At
# least 32 random characters:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# Leaving a placeholder here is refused at boot, deliberately. Do not paste one back in.
OUTBOX_SIGNING_SECRET=

# The upstreams.
#
#   ledger  — every fill posting, every performance fee, every capital reservation. This service
#             holds no balance of its own; see the header of src/ledgerclient.ts.
#   pricing — the mark and the fill price. A rate that cannot be quoted is an ERROR here, never a
#             default, so a bot with no price does not trade.
#   billing — subscription tier and limits. Soft: a last-known tier is served while it is down.
LEDGER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4007
PRICING_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4006
BILLING_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4009

# This service's own scoped credential. NOT shared with any other service — SD-05.
# It must carry: ledger:post, ledger:reserve, ledger:read, pricing:read.
TRADE_SERVICE_TOKEN=

# --- optional, with the defaults shown ---------------------------------------------------------

PORT=4000
NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info
TRADE_DATABASE_POOL_MAX=10

# **THE MONEY KILL SWITCH.** Read on every tick, not at boot and not when a bot is created.
#
# While it is off, no live bot trades and no performance fee is settled. It is deliberately not a
# status change: the intent is to stop money moving, not to unwind everyone's positions, and a bot
# left running resumes the moment it goes back on.
#
# Defaults to FALSE, and that default is the reason docs/ecosystem/17 §9 lists the frozen service's
# performance fee under "a feature behind a flag nobody enabled". Turning it on is a deliberate,
# recorded act.
# TRADE_LIVE_ENABLED=false

# The `fast-read` budget from 07 §2. Applies to pricing and billing.
# TRADE_UPSTREAM_DEADLINE_MS=800

# The `money-write` budget from 07 §2. Applies to the ledger, and carries NO automatic retry: the
# caller re-submits under the same idempotency key when it is ready to.
# TRADE_MONEY_DEADLINE_MS=5000

# The performance-fee accrual period, in seconds.
#
# **A correctness control, not a tuning knob.** A settlement's identity is `(bot_id, period)` where
# period = floor(now / this), and `fee_settlements_bot_period_uniq` is what makes a second charge for
# one period impossible. Shortening it makes fees more frequent; changing it on a running deployment
# re-opens every in-flight period exactly once, so do it during a quiet window.
# TRADE_SETTLEMENT_PERIOD_SECONDS=3600

# Names this replica in jobs.locked_by. Defaults to the hostname, which is the container id under
# compose and the pod name under Kubernetes.
# INSTANCE_ID=

# The image tag, reported on every log line and in the release manifest.
# CLOUDSFORGE_TAG=dev

# --- not read by this service ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT and the rest of OTEL_* are read by the OpenTelemetry SDK loaded ahead
# of the process, not by src/env.ts. They belong in the deploy, not here.
#
# There is NO exchange or market-data credential here, and that is deliberate: this service does not
# fetch prices or candles. Bars arrive through POST /v1/series/:id/bars and rates come from pricing.
# See the header of src/series.ts.
#
# TRADE_TEST_DSN is read only by the test suite, and only when its value contains "test" — the
# database-backed tests truncate. See src/testsupport.ts for why it is not named
# the `<service>_test_database_url` name the other services use.
